## License texts

- `third-party/licenses/mariadb-LGPL-2.1.txt`: unchanged upstream license.
- `third-party/licenses/sqlite-Apache-2.0.txt`: unchanged upstream license.
- `third-party/licenses/sqlite-LICENSE.zentus`: unchanged upstream BSD notice.
- `third-party/licenses/sqlite-NOTICE`: unchanged upstream attribution notice.

The deployment JAR includes these files under `META-INF/item-counters/third-party/`,
and the ItemCounters LICENSE, including these notices, under `META-INF/item-counters/`.
Existing SQLite license files inside the dependency are preserved.

## MariaDB corresponding source and replacing the library

The unmodified matching source archive is available from Maven Central:
[MariaDB Connector/J 3.5.6 sources](https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2/org/mariadb/jdbc/mariadb-java-client/3.5.6/mariadb-java-client-3.5.6-sources.jar).
It contains the driver source and Maven build definition. Upstream source:
https://github.com/mariadb-corporation/mariadb-connector-j/tree/3.5.6

The driver is not modified or relocated in the deployment JAR. ItemCounters
source is available in `src/main/java/`, and its component build definition is
`build.gradle.kts`. For local replacement, select the compatible driver in `build.gradle.kts`
and rebuild `jar` with Java 21 / Gradle 8.14.3.
For a locally modified Connector/J driver, build/install its Maven artifact and
use that artifact in the component build instead of the original Maven dependency.
Keep one driver version in the resulting JAR. Local modification, relinking and
reverse engineering to debug modifications are expressly allowed by the
ItemCounters license. Redistribution of the library itself remains governed
by LGPL, rather than by ItemCounters' resale restrictions.

## SQLite source

https://github.com/xerial/sqlite-jdbc/tree/3.50.3.0

Packaging retains the original x86_64/aarch64 native binaries and removes other
native targets. Driver Java classes are unchanged.

## External dependencies

Purpur/Paper API and PlaceholderAPI are compile-only and are not bundled.
PlaceholderAPI is optional at runtime and is installed separately by the server
administrator. Gson is provided by the Minecraft server for legacy JSON import.
JUnit is test tooling, not part of the plugin JAR.
